f Celestials  appears a little different for example  ego described himself as a brain  floating alone in space eventually  created life around himself  anyway this brings us back to Chronos  now Chronos is an eternal it's a race  created by the Celestials their  evolutionary offshoots of humans with  powers and longer lifespans kind of like  the end humans but not the same thing  now Chronos was an eternal who  experimented with cosmic energy  merging him with time he is the master  of time he can slow down time he can  stop time generally work time you can  put time down  in Reverse time that's pretty bad  Chronos is also thanassis grandfather  they anos along with his father and his  mother are all each Colonels as well  Chronos his son was a Lars who was  actually mentioned by Red Skull infinity  war he greeted that oh says son of  in-laws now Chronos founded Titan that  Stannis is home planet that was  destroyed by overpopulation which was  the major setting in infinity war now  Kronos was a creation by comic book  artist jim Starlin recently Starlin  spoke at a panel in puerto rico where a  reporter quoted him as saying that he  would be receiving a credit for another  one of his marvel creations and Avengers  war and Chronos seemed like the most  obvious pic he's directly related to  Thanos and he controls time which seems  like it would be a useful tool in the  Avengers final battle against Thanos but  but but even more recently jim Starlin  clarified his comments he said that he  was actually misquoted that it came up  that he received two character credits  and Infinity Ward and that he joked that  he would shoot for three in Avengers 4  but let's be honest theories about  Chronos and of interest for began long  before Starlin was misquoted Cronus  could present some really interesting  story possibilities for Avengers 4  imagine a cosmic force intervening in  the Avengers conflict revealing himself  to Tony Stark as Thanos his grandfather  rendering judgment on his mad Titans  grandson so now he's backing the other  side perhaps we'll learn that during  Doctor Strange his glances into those 14  million different futures he communed  with Chronos who counselled strange to  allow events to transpire in a specific  way so that in the end game Chronos  could help a specific line up Avengers  by rewinding them to past conflicts to  reset the timeline in a way to even the  odds against his wayward grandson by the  way after Thanos acquired the time stone  remember Strange told Stark the line  we're in the endgame now and you may  have seen that Avengers endgame came up  recently as a possible title for  Avengers 4 because the cinematographer  on these movies listed Avengers in game  on his official credits before changing  it mysteriously now it's not clear if  endgame was just a working title for the  movie since the Russo brothers have  confirmed that the title for Avengers 4  would not be a line of dialogue from  infinity war Marvel head Kevin Feige has  said that the title would be revealed  after the first trailer for Captain  Marvel  sometime in the next few months but  getting back to Kronos of course cosmic  entities have been used sparingly in the  MCU they're really hard to wrap your  brain around for average viewers and for  nerds honestly but more importantly they  create stakes problems for these movies  when literally the entire universe is at  stake it's kind of hard to understand  the emotional reaction to that from the  character point of view for example as  we saw in Fantastic Four rise of the  Silver Surfer Galactus who is another  cosmic entity was just too huge and  amoral for us to register him as an  intimate emotional threat to the heroes  now guardians vol 2 actually got around  that by making ego really vain and  selfish with a strong emotional  connection to Peter quill and some  really clever exposition scenes to help  clarify his even existence and actor  Kurt Russell displays all of his  characters with a humanity that we all  immediately connect with  so if Chronos does appear in the MCU  they wouldn't be wise to also make him a  quirky human figure that we can relate  to and if we're looking back in the  comics for inspiration here's one fun  idea go meta the most powerful cosmic  entity in the Marvel Comics is a figure  called the one above all he or she here  it is a god-like being whose true form  it's never seen the one above all just  takes various forms then one of those  forms was artist Jack Kirby himself that  comic issue zoomed out from a comic  panel to show him in his studio drawing  Fantastic Four comics it was pretty  awesome so if we're looking at this from  the Marvel Cinematic Universe  wouldn't it be a hoot for that cosmic  entity the one above all or Crono serve  anyone else to be played by Stan Lee  just think about it the guy has already  appeared in pretty much every movie with  Marvel characters and a Guardians vol 2  we actually saw him yucking it up with  these guys now these are called the  Watchers there are also cosmic entities  who observe and record all the events in  the universe and there was actually a  theory going around at the time that  Stan Lee could be uatu the watcher sure  Stan Lee isn't an actor but his many  cameos have made him a familiar face to  everyone who sees these movies and his  appearance as a cosmic entity who  conducts divine intervention with the  Avengers to help them defeat Thanos  could offset any of this cosmic  backstory that could alienate some  viewers so here you have it and the 14  million one odds that Chronos happens to  appear in Avengers 4 and it's played by  Stan Lee you heard it here first but a  question for you guys in Avengers 4  would you prefer this kind of  intervention from a cosmic entity or  should the adventures just handle things  on their own comment down below with  your thoughts or tweet me directly at EA  boss and follow new rockstars on Twitter  for updates on our 